# Project: EJ Blue Collar Intelligence (labor-intelligent-sys)
# Scope: Full-stack monorepo (Flutter frontend + Backend services)

## Core Philosophies (Strict Enforcement)
- **First Principles Thinking:** Break problems down to their most basic, foundational truths. Do not copy bloated boilerplate or build complex abstractions prematurely. Build from the ground up based on absolute requirements.
- **KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid):** Simplicity is our best friend. Avoid over-engineering, unnecessary microservices, overly clever one-liners, or redundant design patterns. Choose the most direct, readable, and maintainable path.


## Git & Identity
- Author identity: dhruval-huntlo <dhruval@huntlo.ai>
- Push target: origin/main on gigkaroonline-svg/EJ_blue_collar_Intelligence

## Monorepo Layout
- /frontend: Flutter application. Follow Dart/Flutter best practices, use structured state management, and do not track build/ or .dart_tool/ artifacts.
- /backend: API services and intelligence layer. Keep business logic modular and enforce strict environment variable separation (.env).

## Coding Guidelines
- Prioritize clean architecture, testable services, and explicit error handling.
- When generating code, follow existing project naming conventions and structure.
